H("871.d.6.E",4,"During a safety meeting, effective listening includes:","taking notes and asking clarifying questions",["texting","talking over others","leaving early"],"Listen actively.")
H("871.d.6.F",3,"A student reads a route map, a bill of lading and a driver's manual and explains what each requires. He is:","reading and comprehending materials common to transportation",["avoiding documents","guessing","skipping details"],"Understand industry documents.")
H("871.d.6.F",4,"A freight dispatcher who misreads a delivery address on a manifest could cause:","a misdelivery and added cost",["faster service","no effect","an early arrival"],"Careful reading prevents errors.")
H("871.d.6.G",3,"Using a manufacturer's service manual, a student writes step-by-step maintenance instructions for a school bus. He is:","employing writing and preparation skills with technical information",["copying jokes","doing nothing","guessing"],"Technical writing is precise.")
H("871.d.6.G",4,"Good technical instructions should be:","clear, ordered and accurate",["vague","random","humorous only"],"Instructions must be usable.")
H("871.d.6.H",3,"A student stands before the class and clearly explains how air brakes work, using visuals and a steady pace. He is demonstrating:","speaking skills",["silence","reading silently","mumbling"],"Present clearly.")
H("871.d.6.H",4,"One way to strengthen a presentation is to:","practice ahead of time and make eye contact with the audience",["read without looking up","speak very fast","skip an outline"],"Practice improves delivery.")
H("871.d.7.A",3,"A company explores new engine designs, route-optimization software and battery chemistries. These are:","major fields of research and development",["unrelated hobbies","decorations","payroll tasks"],"R&D covers many fields.")
H("871.d.7.A",4,"Research and development in transportation often focuses on:","improving safety, efficiency and fuel use",["lowering quality","adding delays","reducing training"],"R&D improves systems.")
H("871.d.7.B",3,"A team forms a question about tire wear, tests two tire types on a test route and records the results. They are:","applying scientific methods of research",["guessing","copying","ignoring data"],"Question, test, analyze.")
H("871.d.7.B",4,"For a fair test of two brake pads, the team should:","change only one variable and keep the rest the same",["change everything at once","skip measuring","test only once"],"Control variables.")
H("871.d.7.C",3,"A student researching a new traffic signal system uses a state DOT report, a university study and an interview with an engineer. She is using:","a variety of resources for research and development",["one source only","no sources","guesses"],"Use several sources.")
H("871.d.7.C",4,"Which source is likely the most reliable for road safety statistics?","a government transportation agency report",["a stranger's comment","an anonymous poster","a rumor"],"Official data is reliable.")
H("871.d.7.D",3,"A researcher states a hypothesis about fuel efficiency, collects data under controlled conditions, analyzes it and draws a conclusion. This describes:","the scientific method of research",["a sales pitch","a guess","a rumor"],"Hypothesis, test, conclusion.")
H("871.d.7.D",4,"A hypothesis in a transportation experiment is:","a testable prediction about the outcome",["a proven fact","a random opinion","a final conclusion"],"Hypotheses are testable.")
H("871.d.8.A",3,"A student presents a plan to install better lighting at a bus depot, explaining the goal, cost and expected safety benefit to the manager. They are:","discussing a project proposal",["avoiding ideas","making no plan","ignoring cost"],"Proposals explain goal, cost and benefit.")
H("871.d.8.A",4,"A strong project proposal for a transportation improvement should include:","the problem, the proposed solution, the cost and the expected benefit",["only a title","only a drawing","only a slogan"],"Proposals are complete.")
